    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nHi,\n\nMaybe I'm just missing it in the docs but often I'm in mini.files and I want to open a file for editing for whatever reason. I have the explorer picker from mini extras too but it just feels kind of wrong to need to open the fuzzy finder when I have the file I want already highlighted in mini.files. Is there a way to press <cr> or something to open the selected file for editing. ",
