            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hello!\n\n> ... I want to open a file for editing for whatever reason\n\nThis is understandable as it is one of the main goals of opening file explorer :)\n\nIt is done via [\"go in\" action](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c122e852517adaf7257688e435369c050da113b1/doc/mini-files.txt#L153) which is `l` by default. It either goes inside directory or opens a file (i.e. \"goes inside file\"). If you want to open file and close explorer, use [\"go in plus\" action](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c122e852517adaf7257688e435369c050da113b1/doc/mini-files.txt#L155) (`L` by default).",
